{"name":"Stormy Strait Grey","hex":"#6b8ba4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stormy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to storms.","Characterized by, or proceeding from, a storm; subject to storms; agitated with strong winds and heavy rain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stormy"},{"term":"strait","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Narrow; restricted as to space or room; close.","Righteous, strict."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A narrow channel of water connecting two larger bodies of water.","A narrow pass, passage or street."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strait"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Strait","blocks":[{"text":"A strait is a water body connecting two seas or water basins. The surface water is, for the most part, at the same elevation on both sides and can flow through the strait in either direction, although the topography generally constricts the flow somewhat. In some straits, there is a dominant directional current. Most commonly, the strait is a narrow channel that lies between two land masses. Straits are loci for sediment accumulation, with sand-sized deposits usually occurring on the two strait exits, forming subaqueous fans or deltas. Some straits are not navigable because they are too narrow, too shallow, or due to the presence of a reef or archipelago."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Strait.svg/330px-Strait.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strait","wikidata":"Q37901"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/ISS-44_Strait_of_Gibraltar.jpg/500px-ISS-44_Strait_of_Gibraltar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/ISS-44_Strait_of_Gibraltar.jpg/1280px-ISS-44_Strait_of_Gibraltar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/ISS-44_Strait_of_Gibraltar.jpg/500px-ISS-44_Strait_of_Gibraltar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Strait of Gibraltar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AISS-44_Strait_of_Gibraltar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Empty_Singapore-Malaysia_Causeway.jpg/500px-Empty_Singapore-Malaysia_Causeway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Empty_Singapore-Malaysia_Causeway.jpg/1280px-Empty_Singapore-Malaysia_Causeway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Empty_Singapore-Malaysia_Causeway.jpg/500px-Empty_Singapore-Malaysia_Causeway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Johor–Singapore Causeway traverses the Strait of Johor. Johor Bahru is in the background.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEm